In the top layer, Ladybird makes a position other than absolute or
fixed compute to absolute, and a display of contents compute to block,
for an element other than the document element and for its ::backdrop.
Blink does the same in StyleAdjuster::AdjustComputedStyle(), for an
element that IsInTopLayer() and for a kPseudoIdBackdrop style. Gecko’s
StyleAdjuster::adjust_for_top_layer() does it for every style with
“-moz-top-layer: auto”, which its UA stylesheet gives every ::backdrop.
And WebKit’s Style::Adjuster::adjust() sets the position for a style
that isInTopLayerOrBackdrop().
